{%- comment -%}
  Instructor row — named faces, horizontal scroll.

  TWO DATA SOURCES, chosen by the `source` setting:

    manual      — hand-entered blocks. Use when there is no metaobject yet.
    metaobject  — loops an existing metaobject type, default `our_team`.

  The metaobject path reads the SAME `our_team` entries that already drive
  templates/page.instructors-list.json. Nothing needs migrating or
  re-populating: the data is already there, the section just reads it.

  Field mapping (all verified present on our_team):
    name           -> card name
    certification  -> cert line
    type           -> meta line   (or client_groups, switchable)
    picture        -> portrait
    system.url     -> link        (or collection_url, switchable)

  Unused here but available: introduction, client_groups, image_1, image_2.

  There is no teaching-locations field on our_team. The meta line falls back
  to `type`, which is not the same thing. Add a field to the definition if
  the distinction matters.

  Later, SSMS owns instructor records. Per PUBLIC_API_PLAN.md the public API
  is server-to-server only (API key held by a Shopify app proxy or app
  server) — Liquid cannot call it directly, and a browser fetch would leak the
  key. So the pipe becomes:

      SSMS  ->  metaobjectUpsert  ->  metaobject  ->  this section

  That sync can write straight into `our_team`. Point SSMS at the existing
  type rather than creating a second one — two instructor types would mean
  two sources of truth and a reconciliation problem nobody asked for.

  Visibility rules live on the SSMS side: only approval_status = 'approved'
  AND is_active = true are ever synced.

  ---- SCALE ----
  A bare loop over shop.metaobjects.instructor.values stops at 50 entries and
  fails SILENTLY — no error, the 51st instructor just is not there. Storage is
  not the constraint (a definition holds 1M entries); this is a render cap.

  It lifts with {% paginate %}, which is officially supported on
  metaobject_definition.values and takes a page size up to 250:

    {%- paginate shop.metaobjects.instructor.values by 250 -%}
      {%- for card in shop.metaobjects.instructor.values -%}
        ...
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endpaginate -%}

  Two rules that are easy to get wrong:
    - Loop the EXPRESSION, not an assign'd copy made outside the block. An
      assign that reads the values before {% paginate %} opens captures the
      unpaginated (50-item) array.
    - Keep the paginate block in the section, not a shared snippet.

  But for THIS section, pagination is the wrong answer. It is a horizontal
  face row — dumping 100+ portraits into it is both a UX and a page-weight
  failure, and a second page of a horizontal rail is meaningless. At that
  roster size this section should render a curated subset (SSMS sets a
  `featured` boolean, or sort by `sort_order` and cap the loop with `limit:`),
  and the full roster belongs on a dedicated paginated instructors page where
  the 250-per-page block is the right tool.

  Also note: addressing entries individually by handle
  (metaobjects.instructor['some-handle']) caps at 20 unique handles per page
  and does NOT paginate at all. Always go through .values.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  TWO stylesheets. instructor.css owns the card internals, shared with the
  roster page through snippets/club-instructor-card.liquid; club.css owns this
  rail's layout. Dropping either leaves the cards half-styled.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'instructor.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'club.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<div class="club-faces color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient">
  <div class="page-width">
    <div class="club-faces__head">
      <div>
        {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
          <p class="club-faces__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="club-faces__title">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- if section.settings.link_label != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ section.settings.link_url | default: '#' }}" class="club-faces__all link">
          {{- section.settings.link_label -}}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <ul class="club-faces__rail" role="list">
    {%- if section.settings.source == 'metaobject' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign roster = shop.metaobjects[section.settings.metaobject_type].values
        assign shown = 0
      -%}

      {%- if roster == blank or roster.size == 0 -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Empty means the type handle is wrong, not that the roster is empty —
          a mistyped handle resolves to nil and renders nothing at all. Show
          the reason in the editor only; storefront visitors get silence.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if request.design_mode -%}
          <li class="club-faces__card">
            <p class="club-faces__name">No entries found</p>
            <p class="club-faces__loc">
              No metaobject type named
              “{{ section.settings.metaobject_type }}”, or it has no entries.
              Check the handle in Settings › Custom data › Metaobjects.
            </p>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- for entry in roster limit: section.settings.limit -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign shown = shown | plus: 1

          if section.settings.meta_field == 'client_groups'
            assign loc = entry.client_groups.value
          else
            assign loc = entry.type.value
          endif

          if section.settings.link_target == 'collection'
            assign url = entry.collection_url.value
          else
            assign url = entry.system.url
          endif
        -%}
        {%- render 'club-instructor-card',
          card_name: entry.name.value,
          card_cert: entry.certification.value,
          card_loc: loc,
          card_image: entry.picture.value,
          card_url: url
        -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- render 'club-instructor-card',
          card_name: block.settings.display_name,
          card_cert: block.settings.certification,
          card_loc: block.settings.teaching_locations,
          card_image: block.settings.profile_photo,
          card_attrs: block.shopify_attributes
        -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </ul>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Club instructors",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "source",
      "label": "Data source",
      "options": [
        { "value": "manual", "label": "Blocks entered below" },
        { "value": "metaobject", "label": "Metaobject entries" }
      ],
      "default": "metaobject",
      "info": "Metaobject reads the same instructor records the instructors page already uses. Nothing to re-enter."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "metaobject_type",
      "label": "Metaobject type handle",
      "default": "our_team",
      "info": "The API handle, not the display name. Find it under Settings › Custom data › Metaobjects. A wrong handle renders nothing at all."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "limit",
      "min": 4,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 2,
      "label": "Maximum shown",
      "default": 12,
      "info": "This is a scrolling row, not a directory — keep it short and link to the full roster. 50 is the hard ceiling for an unpaginated metaobject loop."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "meta_field",
      "label": "Meta line",
      "options": [
        { "value": "type", "label": "Type" },
        { "value": "client_groups", "label": "Client groups" }
      ],
      "default": "type"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "link_target",
      "label": "Card links to",
      "options": [
        { "value": "profile", "label": "Instructor profile page" },
        { "value": "collection", "label": "Their collection" }
      ],
      "default": "profile"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "教练团队"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "带你上雪的人"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "link_label",
      "label": "Link label",
      "default": "全部教练"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "link_url",
      "label": "Link"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Color scheme",
      "default": "background-2"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "instructor",
      "name": "Instructor",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "profile_photo",
          "label": "Profile photo"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "display_name",
          "label": "Display name",
          "default": "教练姓名"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "certification",
          "label": "Certification",
          "default": "CSIA Level 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "teaching_locations",
          "label": "Teaching locations",
          "default": "MSL · Blue Mountain"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Club instructors",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "instructor" },
        { "type": "instructor" },
        { "type": "instructor" },
        { "type": "instructor" },
        { "type": "instructor" },
        { "type": "instructor" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
